# Real-word typo: "barley" (a grain) for "barely". Pattern from published
# lists of mistakes spell-checkers miss; examples are ours.
# why: Barely means only just; barley is a grain. Both are real words, so spell-checkers miss the swap.
expr main [<(barley [any, enough, made, make, able, there, noticeable, noticed, touched, slept, know, knew, passed, managed, legal, visible, audible, breathing, alive, survived, finished, started, even, got, had, been, see, saw, seen, hear, heard, ever, fit, fits, fitted, scraped, recognise, recognize, recognised, recognized, remember, remembered, understand, understood, moved, keep, kept, afford, cover, covers, covered, register, registered, significant, changed, use, used, spoke, speak, said, ate, eat, slept, older, younger, over, under, above, below, out, in, awake, scratched, begun, started, open, opened]), barley>, <([I, (I've), (I'd), he, she, we, they, you, it, was, were, is, are, could, can, (can't), should, would, will, might, may, must, had, have, has, just, so, only] barley [any, enough, made, make, able, there, have, sleep, walk, move, breathe, hear, talk, speak, stand, function, cover, contain, hold, get, pay, manage, cope, slept, know, knew, passed, managed, got, had, see, saw, hear, heard, ever, fit, afford, remember, understand, moved, keep, kept, awake, noticed, alive, breathing, legal, visible, significant, (a), (an), (the), started, finished, slept, spoke, said, eat, ate, use, used, read, opened, open, recognise, recognize]), barley>]

let message "Did you mean `barely`? (`Barley` is a grain.)"
let description "Catches `barley` where `barely` (only just) was meant."
let kind "Typo"
let becomes "barely"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "I barley slept last night." "I barely slept last night."
test "The results were barley significant." "The results were barely significant."
test "We barley made it on time." "We barely made it on time."
test "There was barley enough food." "There was barely enough food."

allows "The farm grows barley and wheat."
allows "Add a cup of pearl barley to the soup."
allows "I barely slept last night."

test "We should barley have enough time." "We should barely have enough time."
test "I could barley sleep." "I could barely sleep."
